The attached image illustrates the comparable adjuvanticity of Nano-11 nanoparticles with aluminum hydroxide (AH) in enhancing anti-recombinant protective antigen (rPA) IgG titers in mice. The box plot shows that both Nano-11 and AH significantly increase antibody responses compared to rPA alone. At higher doses (200 µg and 50 µg), Nano-11 and AH induce similar levels of IgG. Crucially, Nano-11 demonstrates superior immunopotentiation at a lower dose of 12.5 µg, maintaining a robust antibody response comparable to higher adjuvant doses, whereas AH's efficacy significantly diminishes at this concentration. This suggests Nano-11 is an effective vaccine adjuvant, particularly at lower doses.